1
00:00:09,380 --> 00:00:11,120
Lighten up and step back a bit, would you?

2
00:00:20,160 --> 00:00:24,260
Anyone without money, come to my place!

3
00:00:24,260 --> 00:00:29,000
I don't have any either, so don't worry.

4
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:32,820
Look at the blue sky,

5
00:00:33,680 --> 00:00:36,300
white clouds.

6
00:00:37,760 --> 00:00:42,840
Things will work out somehow, eventually.

7
00:00:55,900 --> 00:00:59,920
Anyone without a job, come to my place!

8
00:01:00,580 --> 00:01:04,600
I don't have one either, so don't worry.

9
00:01:41,020 --> 00:01:43,680
Little Ryotsu, the little fairy,

10
00:01:58,020 --> 00:02:00,200
Why is it so hot?

11
00:02:01,760 --> 00:02:03,140
I'm parched.

12
00:02:03,960 --> 00:02:05,680
Guess I'll get some juice.

13
00:02:07,300 --> 00:02:07,540
Mm.

14
00:02:08,980 --> 00:02:09,460
Mm.

15
00:02:10,440 --> 00:02:10,920
Mm.

16
00:02:14,620 --> 00:02:17,280
What am I supposed to buy with ten yen?

17
00:02:17,280 --> 00:02:18,220
Mm.

18
00:02:18,220 --> 00:02:18,900
Mm.

19
00:02:23,820 --> 00:02:25,780
The 10-yen coin got bigger.

20
00:02:30,760 --> 00:02:33,380
Could it be that I've gotten smaller?

21
00:02:33,380 --> 00:02:35,820
That's right, you idiot!

22
00:02:38,440 --> 00:02:40,780
How does it feel to be small?

23
00:02:40,780 --> 00:02:42,720
Are you Hanayama?

24
00:02:44,140 --> 00:02:46,900
You shrank me again, that's a dirty trick!

25
00:02:46,900 --> 00:02:49,120
Shrinking me out of nowhere for no reason!

26
00:02:49,120 --> 00:02:51,220
Did I do something wrong?

27
00:02:51,220 --> 00:02:52,880
It's on a whim.

28
00:02:53,760 --> 00:02:57,740
Your misdeeds have already
accumulated to 600 million points.

29
00:02:57,740 --> 00:02:59,560
600 million points?!

30
00:03:00,340 --> 00:03:02,460
Look at this!

31
00:03:08,660 --> 00:03:10,340
Alright, it's done!

32
00:03:10,860 --> 00:03:14,580
Building it right under the Chief's
nose makes it all the more satisfying.

33
00:03:24,520 --> 00:03:26,860
Take this, you stupid dog!

34
00:03:29,900 --> 00:03:32,600
Stealing someone else's takoyaki?
Everybody does that.

35
00:03:41,820 --> 00:03:44,360
Not sorting the trash properly,
and stuff like that.

36
00:03:44,360 --> 00:03:46,600
Washing your own
underwear at the laundromat.

37
00:03:46,600 --> 00:03:49,280
Cutting one in a crowded elevator.

38
00:03:49,280 --> 00:03:51,380
Obsessing over erotic videos all the time.

39
00:03:51,380 --> 00:03:53,720
Everybody does stuff like that, you know!

40
00:03:54,120 --> 00:03:56,360
You're a police officer,
for crying out loud!

41
00:03:57,520 --> 00:04:00,360
I can't overlook your misdeeds.

42
00:04:01,900 --> 00:04:04,000
You'll reflect on yourself
in that form for a while.

43
00:04:04,720 --> 00:04:06,520
What? Don't mess with me!

44
00:04:06,680 --> 00:04:08,500
You coward, change me back!

45
00:04:08,580 --> 00:04:09,200
You heartless bastard!

46
00:04:09,380 --> 00:04:10,740
Damn old geezer! Useless!

47
00:04:10,860 --> 00:04:11,940
You ringworm-riddled freak!

48
00:04:13,760 --> 00:04:14,720
What are you planning to do?

49
00:04:15,120 --> 00:04:16,260
Old man, stop it!

50
00:04:16,380 --> 00:04:17,000
What are you doing?

51
00:04:21,100 --> 00:04:22,000
No way!

52
00:04:22,520 --> 00:04:23,160
Stop it!

53
00:04:23,160 --> 00:04:26,860
Kyaa, shoot 'em!

54
00:04:28,400 --> 00:04:29,520
You, Keller!

55
00:04:31,060 --> 00:04:33,140
If I say so myself, that was a nice shot.

56
00:04:40,800 --> 00:04:42,380
Whoa, don't!

57
00:04:48,940 --> 00:04:51,260
Damn it, that Section Chief Kobayashi,

58
00:04:51,260 --> 00:04:53,620
blaming his own mistake on me!

59
00:04:54,120 --> 00:04:56,140
Dammit, it makes me so angry!

60
00:04:56,800 --> 00:04:59,320
Damn you, Section Chief Kobayashi!

61
00:04:59,920 --> 00:05:00,840
Not again!

62
00:05:07,560 --> 00:05:08,280
Uh-oh.

63
00:05:09,840 --> 00:05:10,740
Dammit.

64
00:05:14,760 --> 00:05:17,060
Phew, I nearly died there.

65
00:05:27,600 --> 00:05:29,160
I barely survived.

66
00:05:30,240 --> 00:05:31,800
Damn, what a mess.

67
00:05:31,800 --> 00:05:35,100
There's nobody but Hanayama
who can change me back.

68
00:05:35,100 --> 00:05:38,000
But I refuse to bow my head no matter what.

69
00:05:40,220 --> 00:05:42,440
Something smells burnt.

70
00:05:43,760 --> 00:05:46,000
Aaaaaaah!

71
00:05:47,940 --> 00:05:48,660
Phew, saved.

72
00:05:50,220 --> 00:05:54,680
Damn it, doesn't the guy who tossed that
cigarette butt get punished by heaven?

73
00:05:58,320 --> 00:06:00,000
So where should we meet?

74
00:06:01,760 --> 00:06:03,640
A once-in-a-lifetime chance.

75
00:06:05,120 --> 00:06:06,180
I slept well.

76
00:06:06,180 --> 00:06:07,760
Fine, let's just do it there then.

77
00:06:12,600 --> 00:06:14,200
Isn't that a little dangerous?

78
00:06:14,720 --> 00:06:29,320


79
00:06:29,320 --> 00:06:31,420
Is that gum?! Are you a cockroach or what?!

80
00:06:40,180 --> 00:06:45,360
Normally it's just a few minutes' walk,
but now that I'm tiny, it's endlessly far.

81
00:06:46,180 --> 00:06:47,420
Guess I'll take a little break.

82
00:06:50,320 --> 00:06:52,900
Help!

83
00:07:01,260 --> 00:07:07,820
Nooo, I finally escaped, but I've gone
even farther from the police box again!

84
00:07:08,580 --> 00:07:10,080
Aaaaaah!

85
00:07:12,160 --> 00:07:20,560
That Ryotsu, loafing around again without doing any work!
If I find him, he's dead meat. He's surely off goofing around somewhere again.

86
00:07:22,260 --> 00:07:24,660
Hey! Chief! Nakagawa! Over here!

87
00:07:24,900 --> 00:07:27,060
It's me! It's me, Chief!

88
00:07:28,000 --> 00:07:29,260
I'm right here, Chief!

89
00:07:29,960 --> 00:07:32,880
Didn't I just hear Ryotsu's voice?

90
00:07:33,020 --> 00:07:35,420
No, I didn't hear anything.

91
00:07:35,420 --> 00:07:37,140
Oh well, must have been my imagination.

92
00:07:39,240 --> 00:07:41,360
Chief, that's too much...

93
00:08:07,120 --> 00:08:07,840
Hey, hey

94
00:08:09,400 --> 00:08:10,840
Instead of reading that book,

95
00:08:11,200 --> 00:08:12,660
why don't you play soccer with me?

96
00:08:16,200 --> 00:08:18,580
Um, that, I, I...

97
00:08:20,880 --> 00:08:21,360
What?

98
00:08:25,160 --> 00:08:28,420
Ugh, I'm useless. What should I do?

99
00:08:30,180 --> 00:08:31,560
I'm done for. I'm really done for.

100
00:08:31,920 --> 00:08:34,980
I'm starving. I'm exhausted.
I can't move anymore.

101
00:08:44,440 --> 00:08:47,000
Could you be a real fairy, by any chance?

102
00:08:57,800 --> 00:08:59,520
So it was all a dream after all.

103
00:08:59,520 --> 00:09:00,820
Well, of course it was.

104
00:09:00,820 --> 00:09:03,220
I'm not letting him shrink me
down over and over like that!

105
00:09:07,160 --> 00:09:08,120
What is this?

106
00:09:11,440 --> 00:09:12,680
No way...

107
00:09:14,980 --> 00:09:16,780
Where am I?

108
00:09:21,520 --> 00:09:22,780
I'm awake.

109
00:09:22,780 --> 00:09:25,380
Who are you? Where is this place?

110
00:09:26,680 --> 00:09:27,700
I'm Shoichi.

111
00:09:27,700 --> 00:09:29,500
This is my room.

112
00:09:29,500 --> 00:09:32,820
You were lying there starving,
so I brought you home, Mr. Fairy.

113
00:09:32,820 --> 00:09:35,260
Hey, are you calling me a fairy?

114
00:09:35,420 --> 00:09:35,700
Mm.

115
00:09:37,220 --> 00:09:40,580
Look, he's exactly like
the fairy in this book!

116
00:09:40,580 --> 00:09:42,380
Nah, no way.
He doesn't look anything like it.

117
00:09:42,380 --> 00:09:44,800
No matter how you look at it,
he's not alike at all.

118
00:09:46,840 --> 00:09:50,360
Fairies have to keep their
true identity a secret, right?

119
00:09:50,720 --> 00:09:52,000
It says so in the book.

120
00:09:53,500 --> 00:09:56,020
I've had enough of this. I'm going home.

121
00:09:57,320 --> 00:10:03,280
We're on the 32nd floor.

122
00:10:03,680 --> 00:10:06,720
Tell me sooner! If I fell, I'd be dead!

123
00:10:07,440 --> 00:10:09,680
Can't fairies fly?

124
00:10:09,820 --> 00:10:10,700
I'm not a fairy.

125
00:10:13,940 --> 00:10:16,660
You were hungry, weren't you?

126
00:10:16,660 --> 00:10:18,440
Eat this.

127
00:10:20,620 --> 00:10:22,440
Can I really eat this?

128
00:10:22,440 --> 00:10:23,080
Yeah.

129
00:10:24,000 --> 00:10:24,780
So

130
00:10:25,320 --> 00:10:27,080
In return

131
00:10:27,400 --> 00:10:28,780
Well, that...

132
00:10:29,560 --> 00:10:30,080
That...

133
00:10:32,020 --> 00:10:32,780
Me and...

134
00:10:32,780 --> 00:10:35,560
Would you be friends with me?

135
00:10:35,560 --> 00:10:37,000
Friends?

136
00:10:37,000 --> 00:10:38,040
Yeah.

137
00:10:38,040 --> 00:10:39,560
I'll give you food too,

138
00:10:39,560 --> 00:10:41,800
and I'll let you eat
my school lunch at noon.

139
00:10:42,280 --> 00:10:43,220
Hey, no way.

140
00:10:45,060 --> 00:10:47,660
I don't have time to be lounging
around in a place like this,

141
00:10:47,660 --> 00:10:50,460
but in this body,
I'm pretty helpless at everything.

142
00:10:50,460 --> 00:10:53,360
If I stick with this kid,
I can eat for free.

143
00:10:54,120 --> 00:10:56,780
Fine, I'll stay here a little longer.

144
00:10:56,780 --> 00:10:58,280
Thank you so much.

145
00:11:00,160 --> 00:11:02,640
What's wrong?
Come on, you're not keeping up at all!

146
00:11:07,160 --> 00:11:08,560
Whoa, it's the preliminaries,
that's amazing!

147
00:11:13,220 --> 00:11:14,160
Shoot!

148
00:11:14,160 --> 00:11:15,260
Go!

149
00:11:15,880 --> 00:11:16,720
Yay!

150
00:11:18,420 --> 00:11:21,360
What, you're totally hopeless!
You're no match for me.

151
00:11:21,940 --> 00:11:24,960
Sorry, this is my first
time playing against someone.

152
00:11:25,460 --> 00:11:28,320
What, have you been
playing this all by yourself?

153
00:11:28,320 --> 00:11:29,120
Yeah.

154
00:11:29,120 --> 00:11:32,900
Yeah... well, I guess it can't be helped.

155
00:11:32,900 --> 00:11:34,780
Alright, let's play again.

156
00:11:34,780 --> 00:11:36,040
Really?

157
00:11:36,040 --> 00:11:36,160
Really?

158
00:11:36,480 --> 00:11:39,040
Yeah, it's a thank-you for buying me dinner.

159
00:11:39,460 --> 00:11:42,400
I'll also teach you a
trick to win this game.

160
00:11:42,400 --> 00:11:46,200
Wow, really?
As expected of a fairy, you know everything!

161
00:11:46,200 --> 00:11:48,140
I already told you, I'm not a fairy!

162
00:12:05,280 --> 00:12:06,080
So sleepy.

163
00:12:06,080 --> 00:12:08,340
Being an elementary schooler is tough

164
00:12:08,340 --> 00:12:10,560
Getting up at this hour every morning,

165
00:12:10,560 --> 00:12:11,660
wow.

166
00:12:12,060 --> 00:12:14,040
Fairies are bad at mornings

167
00:12:14,040 --> 00:12:14,680
What?

168
00:12:15,080 --> 00:12:15,720
Listen.

169
00:12:15,720 --> 00:12:17,380
I've told you a dozen times since yesterday,

170
00:12:18,140 --> 00:12:19,540
I'm not a woman!

171
00:12:20,040 --> 00:12:22,100
Yeah, our little secret, then.

172
00:12:22,920 --> 00:12:23,400
So

173
00:12:26,000 --> 00:12:27,300
Ahaha

174
00:12:27,880 --> 00:12:29,000
Ahaha

175
00:12:29,000 --> 00:12:31,280
Shoichi, good morning.

176
00:12:31,280 --> 00:12:33,360
Uh

177
00:12:33,360 --> 00:12:34,260
Uuugh...

178
00:12:35,800 --> 00:12:36,940
Shall we go?

179
00:12:37,920 --> 00:12:38,400
Hey.

180
00:12:39,680 --> 00:12:41,500
You could at least answer him.

181
00:12:41,500 --> 00:12:44,620
But I... I can't talk well...

182
00:12:45,140 --> 00:12:46,540
It's kind of embarrassing...

183
00:12:48,140 --> 00:12:49,760
My voice just suddenly stops coming out.

184
00:12:50,640 --> 00:12:52,300
Shoichi, you know,

185
00:12:52,300 --> 00:12:53,740
that's exactly why

186
00:12:53,740 --> 00:12:55,420
you don't have any friends, do you?

187
00:12:56,060 --> 00:12:58,720
They're talking to you first, after all.

188
00:12:59,460 --> 00:13:01,760
All you have to do is answer them, isn't it?

189
00:13:01,760 --> 00:13:03,420
But still, I...

190
00:13:04,180 --> 00:13:05,700
Hey, what am I supposed to do?

191
00:13:06,520 --> 00:13:07,240
I know.

192
00:13:07,240 --> 00:13:09,940
Maybe the fairy's magic
could fix it somehow?

193
00:13:11,080 --> 00:13:12,540
I can do stuff like that.

194
00:13:13,120 --> 00:13:16,220
Making friends with magic wouldn't count for anything,
you know.

195
00:13:16,940 --> 00:13:17,660
Yeah, you're right.

196
00:13:18,960 --> 00:13:20,440
What should I do, I wonder?

197
00:13:25,760 --> 00:13:29,240
Okay, okay, I'll help you out.

198
00:13:29,240 --> 00:13:29,980
Really?

199
00:13:29,980 --> 00:13:31,740
Leave it to me.

200
00:13:32,300 --> 00:13:34,640
But listen, I'll help you,

201
00:13:34,640 --> 00:13:38,360
but whether you make friends
or not is up to you. Got it?

202
00:13:41,680 --> 00:13:43,600
Is Ryotsu coming in today too?

203
00:13:44,160 --> 00:13:47,800
Apparently he hasn't gone
home since yesterday, either.

204
00:13:48,560 --> 00:13:50,840
I haven't heard anything
about him going on a trip.

205
00:13:51,360 --> 00:13:53,680
But for him to suddenly
disappear like that...

206
00:13:53,680 --> 00:13:55,360
I wonder if something happened.

207
00:13:57,220 --> 00:13:59,920
He's probably loafing around somewhere again,
no doubt.

208
00:13:59,920 --> 00:14:02,540
Honestly, he's really gotten lax lately.

209
00:14:02,540 --> 00:14:06,480
I'll have to give him a thorough
lecture and knock some sense into him.

210
00:14:09,060 --> 00:14:10,400
Right, let's go!

211
00:14:11,400 --> 00:14:11,720
Yeah.

212
00:14:19,500 --> 00:14:22,700
Operation One, the morning greeting!

213
00:14:22,700 --> 00:14:23,100
Yeah.

214
00:14:27,720 --> 00:14:28,680
Good morning.

215
00:14:34,380 --> 00:14:38,120
That's just saying "good morning," you know!

216
00:14:38,720 --> 00:14:41,560
Are you listening? Hey! At least answer me!

217
00:14:45,980 --> 00:14:48,300
I've never been this nervous before.

218
00:14:51,060 --> 00:14:52,760
Okay, who can solve this problem?

219
00:14:53,560 --> 00:14:58,480
Come on, Operation Two!

220
00:14:58,480 --> 00:15:00,920
Raise your hand over and over
and stand out during class!

221
00:15:00,920 --> 00:15:02,460
Hurry up and raise your hand!

222
00:15:03,520 --> 00:15:05,360
But it's still embarrassing...

223
00:15:05,360 --> 00:15:07,580
I told you I won't tolerate any whining!

224
00:15:08,400 --> 00:15:08,760
But...

225
00:15:08,760 --> 00:15:09,460
But...

226
00:15:09,460 --> 00:15:12,980
Ugh, this is so frustrating!

227
00:15:16,660 --> 00:15:18,920
You're the cat from yesterday!

228
00:15:19,300 --> 00:15:20,900
Then last, Miyahara!

229
00:15:21,860 --> 00:15:23,560
It didn't work after all...

230
00:15:23,560 --> 00:15:26,860
This is no time for that!
Do something about that thing!

231
00:15:38,760 --> 00:15:40,120
Aaaaaah!

232
00:15:41,120 --> 00:15:43,440
What's that cat doing here?

233
00:15:49,360 --> 00:15:54,660
Okay, plan number three: invite everyone during break time.
*raises hand* Yes!

234
00:15:54,660 --> 00:15:55,060
Mm.

235
00:15:59,920 --> 00:16:01,880
What's wrong? Hurry up and go!

236
00:16:01,880 --> 00:16:04,320
Move, Giant Shoichi!

237
00:16:05,220 --> 00:16:07,300
But I'm still so embarrassed.

238
00:16:07,300 --> 00:16:11,380
Idiot! That's exactly why
you can't make any friends!

239
00:16:12,100 --> 00:16:15,020
Nothing will work unless you do it yourself.

240
00:16:15,020 --> 00:16:18,060
I know, I know, but my body just won't -

241
00:16:19,880 --> 00:16:21,340
Hey, lend me the ball.

242
00:16:21,340 --> 00:16:22,040
Thanks.

243
00:16:22,040 --> 00:16:22,800
Thanks.

244
00:16:23,980 --> 00:16:27,420
Hey! What are you doing?!
Are you even trying?!

245
00:16:27,840 --> 00:16:29,500
B-but...

246
00:16:29,500 --> 00:16:32,000
Whoa, that's wild!

247
00:16:33,340 --> 00:16:36,140
I'm busy right now, later!

248
00:16:36,140 --> 00:16:37,740
Listen, Shoichi.

249
00:16:38,380 --> 00:16:40,960
Ugh, how many times do I have to say it?
I'm right now...

250
00:16:41,500 --> 00:16:42,940
Whoa!

251
00:16:43,100 --> 00:16:45,653
Hey, hey, quit poking my nose,

252
00:16:45,703 --> 00:16:47,360
Help me!

253
00:16:47,840 --> 00:16:48,880
Over here!

254
00:16:51,240 --> 00:16:52,060
Fairy-san!

255
00:16:53,680 --> 00:16:55,440
Hey!

256
00:16:56,380 --> 00:16:57,220
Hic!

257
00:17:02,260 --> 00:17:04,220
Fairy-san! Are you okay?

258
00:17:04,800 --> 00:17:06,600
Mm, somehow.

259
00:17:07,260 --> 00:17:08,620
Mm, mm.

260
00:17:08,620 --> 00:17:12,380
Even though you're the one who got helped,
you're really pathetic, you know.

261
00:17:12,840 --> 00:17:15,080
In the end, you couldn't do anything at all.

262
00:17:15,080 --> 00:17:16,040
Y-yeah.

263
00:17:16,960 --> 00:17:20,660
Do you really think you'll make
friends if you just keep running away?

264
00:17:21,460 --> 00:17:24,100
All you have to do is say one word to them.

265
00:17:24,100 --> 00:17:26,540
Then you can play with everyone.

266
00:17:26,540 --> 00:17:29,720
If you can't even do that,
you'll be alone for the rest of your life.

267
00:17:30,500 --> 00:17:37,340
That's fine.
I don't need any friends anymore.

268
00:17:37,880 --> 00:17:42,740
Because I've got you, Mr. Fairy.
You're the best.

269
00:17:43,380 --> 00:17:49,500
With Mr. Fairy here, I'm not alone! Hey,
you'll stay by my side like this forever, right?

270
00:17:49,500 --> 00:17:50,560
Don't mess with me!

271
00:17:50,560 --> 00:17:57,500
I've never seen anyone with as little drive as you.
Friends? Don't make me laugh.

272
00:17:59,480 --> 00:18:01,460
I don't care about you anymore.

273
00:18:01,460 --> 00:18:02,480
See ya.

274
00:18:03,620 --> 00:18:05,040
Some fairy you are.

275
00:18:07,480 --> 00:18:09,000
Y-you, Mr. Fairy...

276
00:18:10,520 --> 00:18:12,560
Okay, who can read this kanji?

277
00:18:21,340 --> 00:18:24,080
Wait... what a pathetic guy you are.

278
00:18:24,080 --> 00:18:27,360
I should have gone home right away
instead of bothering with a guy like that.

279
00:18:37,020 --> 00:18:40,320
See, he's exactly like
the fairy in this book!

280
00:18:40,980 --> 00:18:42,600
You were hungry, weren't you?

281
00:18:43,380 --> 00:18:44,320
Eat this.

282
00:18:44,320 --> 00:18:46,300
Wow, fairy, that's amazing.

283
00:18:47,040 --> 00:18:49,820
Sorry, this is my first
time doing this with someone.

284
00:18:53,580 --> 00:18:54,880
Okay, line up, line up.

285
00:18:58,740 --> 00:18:59,460
Let's eat!

286
00:19:02,680 --> 00:19:05,960
School lunches these days are
just like family restaurant lunches

287
00:19:07,140 --> 00:19:09,780
You came back, fairy?

288
00:19:11,300 --> 00:19:14,640
Well, we had a deal that
you'd let me eat school lunch.

289
00:19:15,220 --> 00:19:16,040
Right, we did.

290
00:19:17,040 --> 00:19:20,520
Once you've eaten, show some guts this time.

291
00:19:20,920 --> 00:19:21,280
Okay.

292
00:19:28,400 --> 00:19:31,520
Listen, Matsuichi, this is our last plan.

293
00:19:31,520 --> 00:19:34,760
The one who shines in PE becomes the class hero,
you know.

294
00:19:34,760 --> 00:19:37,500
So put your heart into
it and nail that shot!

295
00:19:37,500 --> 00:19:37,820
Okay.

296
00:19:38,460 --> 00:19:39,240
B-but...

297
00:19:39,240 --> 00:19:40,220
But what?

298
00:19:40,220 --> 00:19:42,300
I'm bad at sports, though.

299
00:19:42,300 --> 00:19:45,020
I taught you yesterday, didn't I?
It's the same as the game version.

300
00:19:45,020 --> 00:19:46,560
Don't take your eyes off the ball.

301
00:19:46,560 --> 00:19:48,100
Leave the rest to me.

302
00:19:48,100 --> 00:19:49,020
But...

303
00:19:50,820 --> 00:19:51,060
Here it comes!

304
00:19:51,460 --> 00:19:51,860
Whoa!

305
00:19:52,800 --> 00:19:53,440
Whoa!

306
00:19:55,140 --> 00:19:58,140
You idiot! What are you receiving like that?
Trap it properly!

307
00:19:58,900 --> 00:19:59,840
B-but...

308
00:19:59,840 --> 00:20:02,140
Stop your whining and chase the ball!

309
00:20:02,700 --> 00:20:03,020
Yes!

310
00:20:07,260 --> 00:20:08,700
Yes! Caught up! Good!

311
00:20:11,080 --> 00:20:11,740
Here it comes!

312
00:20:13,640 --> 00:20:14,140
Got it!

313
00:20:14,440 --> 00:20:15,780
Right! Triple dash! Oichi!

314
00:20:16,240 --> 00:20:16,560
Yeah!

315
00:20:22,200 --> 00:20:24,300
Three in front, go left!

316
00:20:25,900 --> 00:20:27,420
That's it, Shoichi!

317
00:20:27,420 --> 00:20:28,500
Stop!

318
00:20:29,220 --> 00:20:29,680
Right!

319
00:20:30,820 --> 00:20:31,280
Left!

320
00:20:32,060 --> 00:20:33,500
That guy's amazing.

321
00:20:33,500 --> 00:20:34,280
No kidding.

322
00:20:34,280 --> 00:20:35,700
He got past him again.

323
00:20:35,700 --> 00:20:38,220
Get past him again!

324
00:20:38,220 --> 00:20:39,620
Can you hear me?

325
00:20:39,620 --> 00:20:41,580
Everyone's cheering you on!

326
00:20:41,580 --> 00:20:42,140
Yeah.

327
00:20:49,660 --> 00:20:50,700
Wow.

328
00:20:51,820 --> 00:20:54,520
Aaaaah! Okay, trap it and shoot!

329
00:20:54,520 --> 00:20:56,860
Eeeeeh!

330
00:20:56,860 --> 00:20:58,240
Me.

331
00:21:00,140 --> 00:21:01,800
Aaaaah!

332
00:21:01,800 --> 00:21:02,240
Aaaaah!

333
00:21:02,240 --> 00:21:03,420
Aaaaah!

334
00:21:03,420 --> 00:21:04,480
Eeeeeh!

335
00:21:10,080 --> 00:21:12,020
Aaaaah!

336
00:21:19,680 --> 00:21:20,400
It went in!

337
00:21:20,400 --> 00:21:21,640
Shoichi

338
00:21:24,820 --> 00:21:26,080
That was amazing, Shoichi-kun!

339
00:21:26,080 --> 00:21:28,320
I've never seen dribbling like that before.

340
00:21:28,320 --> 00:21:30,520
You were hiding that you're good at soccer

341
00:21:33,140 --> 00:21:34,580
It was just a fluke.

342
00:21:38,180 --> 00:21:39,020
Fairy-san.

343
00:21:40,360 --> 00:21:43,220
Did you come here to make friends for me?

344
00:21:45,540 --> 00:21:46,760
Thank you, Fairy-san.

345
00:21:47,600 --> 00:21:50,500
Alright, the game's restarting!
Hurry, hurry!

346
00:21:50,500 --> 00:21:51,260
Yeah.

347
00:22:04,980 --> 00:22:08,300
That guy sure knows how to pull off a stylish move,
doesn't he?

348
00:22:09,020 --> 00:22:10,740
I suppose it's about time I changed back.

349
00:22:24,840 --> 00:22:27,240
This is it, we're really in trouble.

350
00:22:37,400 --> 00:22:39,760
He's back! He's back to normal!

351
00:22:39,760 --> 00:22:41,140
Bazaai!

352
00:22:53,020 --> 00:22:55,600
Where on earth did Ryo-chan really go?

353
00:22:56,440 --> 00:22:59,420
I wonder if he got caught
up in some big incident.

354
00:23:01,460 --> 00:23:02,640
That can't be.

355
00:23:02,640 --> 00:23:08,180
Knowing him, he's probably racking his brain right
now for an excuse for skipping work without permission.

356
00:23:08,600 --> 00:23:11,020
When he comes back, this time, for real,

357
00:23:11,020 --> 00:23:11,700
Chief

358
00:23:12,400 --> 00:23:13,460
Ryo-chan

359
00:23:14,020 --> 00:23:14,780
Chief

360
00:23:14,780 --> 00:23:17,660
Chief! Reiko! Nakagawa!

361
00:23:18,880 --> 00:23:19,720
Ryo-chan!

362
00:23:20,040 --> 00:23:20,720
Senpai!

363
00:23:21,180 --> 00:23:23,020
Chief!

364
00:23:24,180 --> 00:23:26,220
Ryo-chan!

365
00:23:31,200 --> 00:23:32,980
You big idiot!

366
00:23:33,760 --> 00:23:37,100
You've been lying to us this whole time!

367
00:23:37,720 --> 00:23:39,820
Chief, there's a reason for this!

368
00:23:40,380 --> 00:23:41,980
I won't hear any of it!

369
00:23:41,980 --> 00:23:44,200
Please hear me out, Chief!

370
00:23:44,780 --> 00:23:45,600
No excuses!

371
00:23:46,680 --> 00:23:47,240
Where?

372
00:23:47,280 --> 00:23:48,180
You were just wandering around!

373
00:23:48,540 --> 00:23:49,360
Whoa, whoa, whoa!

374
00:23:49,400 --> 00:23:50,460
No, listen, listen!

375
00:23:50,580 --> 00:23:51,080
It's not true!

376
00:23:51,180 --> 00:23:53,100
Wow, Shoichi!

377
00:23:53,240 --> 00:23:54,280
It's a hat trick!

378
00:23:54,480 --> 00:23:55,200
It was pure luck!

379
00:23:55,440 --> 00:23:56,420
Let's play soccer again!

380
00:23:56,760 --> 00:23:57,040
Yeah!

381
00:23:57,560 --> 00:23:58,380
Mr. Fairy!

382
00:23:58,380 --> 00:24:00,460
Help me too!

383
00:24:31,160 --> 00:24:34,520
Big busts, small busts,
the small-busted ones, about Yaji's size.

384
00:24:34,520 --> 00:24:35,840
Akisame

385
00:24:35,840 --> 00:24:40,800
Summer has come again this year.

386
00:24:43,700 --> 00:24:46,740
Summer has come again this year.

387
00:24:48,960 --> 00:24:52,320
Big waves, small waves,
the small waves, about Yaji's size.

388
00:24:52,320 --> 00:24:58,240
Big bottoms, small bottoms,
the small ones, about Yaji's size.

389
00:24:58,380 --> 00:24:59,580
Nagisane

390
00:24:59,580 --> 00:25:27,500
Bouncy, bouncy, bouncy, bouncy, bouncy, bouncy, bouncy, bouncy, bouncy, bouncy, bouncy, bouncy, bouncy, bouncy,
bouncy, bouncy, bouncy, bouncy, bouncy, bouncy, bouncy, bouncy, bouncy, bouncy, bouncy, bouncy, bouncy, bouncy, bouncy...

391
00:25:29,900 --> 00:25:31,240
What a cursed camera!

392
00:25:31,240 --> 00:25:35,000
If you don't take 100 sacrilegious
swimsuit photos within a week,

393
00:25:35,000 --> 00:25:36,400
I'll be doomed with misfortune!

394
00:25:37,240 --> 00:25:38,620
Heh, that's easy!

395
00:25:38,620 --> 00:25:39,720
Just you wait.

396
00:25:39,720 --> 00:25:41,400
Photos just as you wish.

397
00:25:41,400 --> 00:25:43,620
I'll shoot and shoot and keep on shooting!

398
00:25:43,620 --> 00:25:46,700
Get those swimsuit photos next time!

399
00:25:47,180 --> 00:25:47,760
Take care.

400
00:25:51,080 --> 00:25:54,120
Autumn, Kameari!

401
00:25:55,300 --> 00:25:59,240
Everyone, come to our town!

402
00:26:00,180 --> 00:26:00,880
Thank you.

